+provenance — but a reader should treat the agent results here as *this format,
+measured by this laboratory*. The gates, fixtures and committed run artifacts have
+now been re-measured by a second laboratory, which also ran 12 fresh isolated
+agent trials of its own (next paragraph). Those trials used one model family;
+external validity across implementers outside that family rests on rounds 4 to 9.
+
+**A second laboratory.** An independent replicator (Y. Puyam) re-ran the public
+parts of the protocol from a fresh clone on a separate machine (Windows 11 Home,
+Rust 1.98.0 MSVC, Python 3.10 and 3.13, Blender 4.2.1 LTS), with no access to
+this laboratory's environment. *Fixtures.* All six Table 17 fixtures, the three
+experiment packages (`mini-v1`, `selfrun-v1`, `smiley-v1`) and the eight CC0
+fixtures matched their published SHA-256 values. All four CC0 builders were
+deterministic on that host; their rebuilds differed from the shipped files only
+in the three spec files with historical CRLF line endings, plus the manifest and
+signature that record them (ruling R1). Three packages went further and rebuilt
+byte for byte from the inputs they embed: `crate-v1` and its damaged twin (180 of
+180 entries), and `ista-varun-v1` (77 of 77, with three stated substitutions), so
+the Gate 9 builder clause that R3 scopes to this laboratory is reproducible from
+the package. `gsplat-v1`, rebuilt from its embedded source, matched in 71 of 83
+entries, including both payloads; the other 12 differ in the R1 spec snapshot,
+the manifest and signature, and recorded host metadata. *Gates.* Golden fixture
+10 PASS, 0 FAIL. Retarget 23 PASS, the UE-rig clauses skipped (non-redistributable
+source). Image profile 14 PASS. Splat 15 PASS, including byte-identical
+self-regeneration from the package's own embedded tools. Enrichment pipeline 19
+PASS on in-repository inputs. Blender adapter 20 PASS, 0 FAIL, 0 SKIP. Unreal
+engine-free core 10 PASS. Public CC0 gates 14, 9 and 8 PASS. Store suite 58
+passed, one skipped (private corpus). Every FAIL on that machine had one of two
+causes: the host's application-control policy blocking freshly built unsigned
+executables, or a clause whose input only this laboratory holds. *Experiment
+artifacts.* The hardcopy generators reproduced `smiley-v1.werk`, `smiley.png` and
+the degraded scan `page-01.jpg` byte for byte, and the control decoder recovered
+the package with 0 of 4096 pixels different on both arms. A blind re-grade wrote
+its criteria from the task prompts and grader source before reading any
+published verdict, then re-executed every committed program it could in a clean
+directory. It agreed with 30 of 39 published verdicts. Six of the nine
+disagreements are a criteria difference: the published grade scores extracted
+bytes, while the stricter reading also scores the listing and per-file
+verification clauses of the task sentence. One is a grader limitation (exact
+colours printed as fractions of 255 instead of integers), and two are
+host-dependent. *Agents.* The second laboratory ran 12 fresh agent trials (Claude
+Code CLI, `claude-opus-5-5`), each in an empty directory holding only the fixture,
+graded by artifact and re-run in a clean directory. Round-1 task: 7 of 7 passed
+(1 on `crate-tex-v1`, 3 on `mini-v1`, 3 on the pinned `crate-v1` with the round-1
+sentence verbatim), with mesh and sound byte-exact in every run. Envelope task on
+`mini-v1`: 3 of 3 decoded every value exactly. Splat task on `gsplat-v1`: 2 of 2,
+with positions and colours matching the fixture on all 281 498 points. No run
+executed or ported a bundled reader. One early run read back its own spilled tool
+output from the harness's configuration directory (outside its workspace, but
+holding only package text); the later trials were sealed, and three equivalent
+attempts were then blocked. Independently, all four agents in the first batch
+found the stale `input_hash` the fixture actually carries, and the runs exposed an
+unspecified case (a `requires` edge to an absent node) on which they chose four
+different behaviours. A pre-registered negative control in the same harness
+(FBX, glTF and USDZ files carrying the same crate) separated werk from the
+controls on its frozen pass rate only through the rule that defines "the primary
+mesh"; with a value-exact single sub-mesh accepted, glTF and FBX also passed 3 of
+3, and the robust differences were verifiability and the file declaring its own
+primary mesh.
 
