+# Second-lab replication of werk
+
+Replicator: Yuvraj Puyam, working independently of the author's laboratory.
+Period: 2026-08-25 to 2026-10-11.
+Status: consolidated report. Every number below comes from a logged run. Each section names its source and the source's date.
+
+Summary: on a separate Windows 11 machine, every gate clause that public data can drive passed, unless the host's application-control policy blocked an executable. Three fixtures rebuilt byte-identically from inputs that the packages themselves embed. 12 of 12 fresh agent trials passed. Every FAIL on this host came from the application-control policy or from data only the author holds.
+
+## 1. Setup
+
+| item | value |
+|---|---|
+| host | Windows 11 Home 10.0.26200, Smart App Control ON (by decision) |
+| repo | `cronos3k/werk` at `6d547d0`. The first checks (2026-08-25) ran at `cbe7cb1`. The Stage 2 gate, `store/` and `paper/` did not change between the two commits. |
+| Rust | 1.98.0 (stable, MSVC) |
+| C/C++ | MSVC 19.44; MinGW present |
+| Python | 3.10.11, 3.13, 3.14.0; numpy 1.26.4; Pillow 12.3.0 (py3.10) and 11.3.0 (py3.13) |
+| other | Blender 4.2.1 LTS; Git 2.51.0 |
+| access | No access to the author's machines, private drives or environment. Fixtures came from the repo and the `fixtures-v1` release. |
+
+Sources (all logged by the replicator):
+
+| id | source | date |
+|---|---|---|
+| S1 | independent verification report (fresh clone, Stage 2, store, first agent trial) | 2026-08-25 |
+| S2 | CC0 gate replication | 2026-09-22 |
+| S3 | replication log | 2026-09-27 |
+| S4 | replication log (released fixtures, gates A, 6, 9, 12) | 2026-09-30 |
+| S5 | paper numbers check | 2026-10-05 |
+| S6 | fresh-agent trials, batch 1, grading and isolation audit | 2026-10-05 |
+| S7 | blind re-grade, comparison with published verdicts | 2026-10-05, updated by S10 |
+| S8 | store measurements | 2026-10-06 |
+| S9 | fresh-agent trials, batch 2 (sealed), grading and isolation audit | 2026-10-07 |
+| S10 | audit of "unavailable" inputs | 2026-10-11 |
+| S11 | `gsplat-v1` rebuild from its embedded source | 2026-10-11 |
+
