+## 5. Fresh-agent trials
+
+Each trial gave a fresh agent an empty directory with only the fixture and the task prompt. Grading was by artifact: the replicator re-ran each final program in a clean directory and hashed the outputs independently.
+
+### 5.1 Results
+
+| task | fixture | trials | strict verdict | source |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| round 1 | `crate-tex-v1` | 1 | 1 PASS | S1 |
+| round 1 | `mini-v1` | 3 | 3 PASS | S6 |
+| round 1 | `crate-v1` (pinned, round-1 sentence verbatim) | 3 | 3 PASS | S9 |
+| envelope | `mini-v1` | 3 (1 in batch 1, 2 in batch 2) | 3 PASS, all values decoded exactly | S6, S9 |
+| gsplat | `gsplat-v1` | 2 | 2 PASS; positions and colours match on all 281 498 points | S9 |
+| **all** | | **12** | **12 PASS** | |
+
+Round 1 is 7 of 7. Mesh and sound were byte-exact in every round-1 run.
+
+| detail | value | source |
+|---|---|---|
+| model | `claude-opus-5-5` in batches 1 and 2 (Claude Code 2.1.290 and 2.1.292). One model family across all 12 trials. | S6, S9 |
+| bundled readers executed or ported | 0 of 12 | S1, S6, S9 |
+| web requests | 0 | S6, S9 |
+| cost and wall clock, batch 1 (4 trials) | $10.43, 1465.0 s | S6 |
+| cost and wall clock, batch 2 (7 trials) | $18.333, 2643.6 s | S9 |
+| known fixture defect found without being told | stale `input_hash` on `rest-poses` (S-DS-7), 4 of 4 in batch 1 | S6 |
+| unspecified case exposed | a `requires` edge to an absent node; 6 runs on `mini-v1` showed 4 different behaviours | S9 |
+
+Stated limits (from S6 and S9): n is small; one model and one vendor; prior knowledge of zip, glTF and 3DGS is constrained, not ruled out; the envelope count is echoable from an in-file hex dump (S-DS-8), the per-entry floats are not. The `crate-tex-v1` trial (S1) had one harness interruption and was resumed.
+
+### 5.2 Isolation
+
+| batch | harness | CLEAN | ATTEMPTED-BUT-BLOCKED | VIOLATION | source |
+|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| first trial (`crate-tex-v1`) | unsealed | not classified | | | S1 |
+| batch 1 (4 trials) | unsealed, user config | 3 | 0 | 1 (technical) | S6 |
+| batch 2 (7 trials) | sealed: own config dir, read block, deny rules, no MCP | 4 | 3 | 0 | S9 |
+
+The batch-1 violation (r1-t3): the agent read two harness spill files outside its workspace. Claude Code had saved the agent's own oversized tool output there. The content was text from inside the package, so no outside information entered the run. It still counts as a violation by the letter of the constraint.
+
+The batch-2 seal added a deny rule for the config directory. The same spill-file read happened 3 times and was denied each time. The seal check before the batch confirmed that the probes were denied.
+
+Not enforced by the seal: Python, Bash and PowerShell processes run unsandboxed on native Windows. The CLEAN classes for scripts rest on reading every command and every agent-written script.
+
+Full per-trial logs are available on request. Trial transcripts are not committed.
+
+## 6. Blind re-grade
+
+The replicator wrote grading criteria from the task prompts and grader source first. Only then were the published verdicts read. Every committed program that could run was re-executed in a clean directory.
+
+| measure | count | source |
+|---|---:|---|
+| runs graded | 39 | S7, S10 |
+| agree | 30 | S7, S10 |
+| mismatch | 9 | S7 |
+| discarded by protocol, graded by neither side | 5 | S7 |
+
+The S10 audit made the two round-2 runs gradeable (the prompt is quoted verbatim in `gauntlet/RESULTS.md`). Both programs PASS on the current fixture, which is a substitute for the original build. Both agree with the published verdict.
+
+| mismatch cause | runs |
+|---|---:|
+| criteria: the published open-weights grade scores extracted bytes only; the stricter reading also scores the node listing and verification of every declared hash | 4 |
+| labelling: the same failure is PARTIAL in one published record and FAIL in another | 1 |
+| criteria: answer-key contamination (S-DS-8) | 1 |
+| grader: the colour test checks a storage form, not a value (S-DS-6) | 1 |
+| host-dependent | 2 |
+| genuine disagreement on the agent's work | 0 |
+
+In the four criteria cases, the extracted bytes are exact. The difference is only the listing and full-verification clauses.
+
+## 7. Negative control (roundNC)
+
+The pre-registered negative-control round ran the same task on FBX, glTF and USDZ files with the same crate mesh and texture (3 trials per arm, 2026-10-11). On the frozen criteria werk passed 3 of 3 and the controls 0 of 9. That gap rests on rule R5 about "the primary mesh". With a value-exact single sub-mesh accepted, glTF and FBX also pass 3 of 3 and USDZ 1 of 3. The robust differences are verifiability (werk 1.0 cryptographic, USDZ CRC-32 only, FBX and glTF none) and the file declaring its primary mesh. Isolation: 0 violations. Details and all artifacts are in the roundNC pull request (`gauntlet/roundNC/RESULTS-NC.md`).
+
